Abstract = {The genus Inonotus is considered polyphyletic of which the recognized
   genera are Inocutis, Inonotus s. str., Inonotopsis, Mesularia, Onnia,
   and Pseudoinonotus. Twenty-four species of the genus Inonotus s.l. were
   studied in this work based upon the examination of 304 specimens
   deposited on the Herbaria ENCB, MEXU, BCMEX, IBUG, XAL, NY, BPI, and
   ARIZ. In Mexico, we found 24 species, corresponding to 5 of the 6 genera
   segregated. Four of these species are new records: Inocutis rheades
   (Pers.) Fiasson and Niemela, Inonotus arizonicus Gilb., I. porrectus
   Murrill, and I. quercustris M. Blackw. and Gilb. Furthermore, I. rickii
   (Pat.). A. Reid is reported as a teleomorphic state for the rst time in
   North America. A key to identify the Mexican species of Inonotus s.l. is
   presented.},
