Note = {9th Mexican School on Gravitation and Mathematical Physics - Cosmology
   for the 21st Century, Mexican Phys Soc, Gravitat \& Math Phys Div,
   Puerto Vallarta, MEXICO, DEC 03-07, 2012},
Organization = {Mexican Natl Sci \& Technol Council; Mexican Phys Soc; Ctr Res \& Adv
   Studies; Mexican Acad Sci; Iztapalapa Metropolitan Autonomous Univ; Univ
   Guanajuato; Natl Autonomous Univ Mexico; Michoacan Univ San Nicolas
   Hidalgo; Natl Inst Astrophys, Opt, \& Elect},
Abstract = {A geometric perspective on singularity resolution previously applied by
   Corichi and Singh to some loop quantum cosmological models is here
   adopted to investigate the interior geometry of a spherically symmetric
   black hole described by an effective Kantowski-Sachs model which
   includes loop quantum corrections. Central to the analysis is the
   expansion rate entering the Raychauduri equation. Such quantity is here
   studied in three cases differing on how the gap area of full loop
   quantum gravity is incorporated. For the (mu) over bar (1), or improved
   quantization, case we find that the Schwarzschild singularity is
   manifestly resolved. A numerical analysis in this case shows there are
   regimes of gravitational repulsion. The other two cases are currently
   under study.},
