   Gonzalez, Monica del Carmen and Peraza Garzon, Alvaro and Cobian Campos,
   Jose Alfredo},
Editor = {Chova, LG and Martinez, AL and Torres, IC},
Title = {DESIGNING LEARNING OBJECTS EMBEDDED ON A ONLINE LEARNING MANAGEMENT
   SYSTEM FOR PEOPLE WITH DYSLEXIA THAT AFFECTS READING ABILITY},
Booktitle = {6TH INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE OF EDUCATION, RESEARCH AND INNOVATION
   (ICERI 2013)},
Year = {2013},
Pages = {2283-2286},
Note = {6th International Conference on Education, Research and Innovation
   (ICERI), Seville, SPAIN, NOV 18-20, 2013},
Abstract = {The main causes of school learning problems are intellectual factors,
   mental disorders, language, cognitive disorders, emotional problems,
   behavioral problems, physical defects, visual or hearing impairments and
   chronic illnesses. Bakwin H. (1974).
   This research will take place around the condition of dyslexia which
   according to Rose J. (2009) is a learning difficulty that primarily
   affects the skills involved in accurate and fluent word reading and
   spelling. Characteristic features of dyslexia are difficulties in
   phonological awareness, verbal memory and verbal processing speed.
   The Dyslexia is a learning disability that has been well documented and
   have encountered problems that arise from this disease including hearing
   problems, motor, attention deficit among other students suffering from
   an early age and affects the performance in the classroom in a high
   percentage, more specifically in this research we focus on the type of
   condition that affects reading ability declining and encouraging student
   learning. This condition currently known as ``Reading Disorder{''} and
   different types have been identified as the Gnosic-praxis, Dysgraphia,
   Aphasia, Auditory processing disorder.
   This has begun to attract the interest of specialists in the field of
   education since there is much research done on the problem of dyslexia
   but very little that focuses on the development of learning objects that
   operate online and are specialized for students suffering from any type
   of dyslexia.
   Doing a research for the design and development of objects that will
   help this condition together with all its variants is extensive to cover
   so in the present research we focus the most common type, which
   according to statistics from the Mexican Social Security Institute
   (IMSS) is the Reading delay, Gnosicpraxis by developing several object
   types, some examples are: detection of the disease, improvement in
   reading, visual support, etc.. These running through an online platform
   accessible from any point of access from any device.},
